,\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Clean release build from scratch, and I verified everything against the compiled C myself.\\n\\n## Files written\\n- `Cargo.toml` — bin target `driver`\\n- `src/main.rs` (95 lines) — argument validation + array/XOR pipeline\\n- `src/rng.rs` (81 lines) — bit-exact glibc `srand`/`rand` (TYPE_3 additive-feedback, deg 31/sep 3, Schrage seeding, 310 discarded outputs)\\n- `src/strtoul.rs` (76 lines) — byte-level `strtoul(s, &end, 10)` clone (whitespace skip, sign, ERANGE, `endptr`)\\n\\n`c_src/` untouched (verified by md5sum; all experiments used copies in `$TMPDIR`).\\n\\n## Verification against the real C binary\\n| Test | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| Full run, seed 1 (2000 iters) | C `42032659` = Rust `42032659` |\\n| Full run, seed 42 | C `430392287` = Rust `430392287` |\\n| 20 seeds × reduced iters (1 and 3), incl. 0, `UINT_MAX`, >2³¹ seeds | all identical (also vs `gcc -O0`) |\\n| 31 argv edge cases, stdout+stderr+exit code, matched argv[0] via `exec -a` | 31/31 byte-identical |\\n\\n## Faithfulness details preserved\\n- **C bugs/quirks kept:** `driver \\\"\\\"` is *accepted* — glibc `strtoul` reports no-conversion without setting `errno`, `*endptr` is already `'\\\\0'`, so seed becomes 0 (then glibc's `srand` silently maps 0→1, so `\\\"\\\"`, `0`, `-0`, `-0000`, and `1` all print the same value). Validation order (`*endptr` → `errno` → `> UINT_MAX`) is unchanged.\\n- **Signed overflow UB** reproduced as two's-complement wrapping (`wrapping_mul/add/sub/shl`), with arithmetic `>>` and C truncate-toward-zero `/` and `%`; `overflow-checks = false` in the release profile.\\n- **Non-UTF-8 argv** is echoed as raw bytes via `OsStrExt`, matching `printf(\\\"%s\\\")`; `argc == 0` renders `(null)` as glibc does.\\n- No stdin is read by this program, so no scanf/fgets semantics apply.\\n\\nTwo notes: `cargo clippy --release` is warning-free, and runtime is inherently ~4–5 min per run (52 billion inner iterations) — the same as the