{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6ibddizgkayazfhxuajdo5s557mmjedqrjbpfuwjvqc63qzv6sta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases passed, and I found and fixed one real translation bug.\n\n## What the code is\n\n`c_src/src/main.c` (82 lines): `driver <seed>` validates the seed with `strtoul`, fills a 1 MB global `int array[262144]` with `rand()`, applies a 100-step integer transformation to every element 2000 times, and prints the XOR of the array. Compiled as a `.so`, it exports exactly three symbols: `array`, `main`, `perform_expensive_operations`.\n\n## Restructuring needed to test it\n\nThe crate was bin-only with no exported symbols, so I added `src/lib.rs` (cdylib) exporting the same three symbols, moved the shared logic into `src/program.rs` (used verbatim by both the bin and the cdylib), and added a `build.rs` that compiles the C into `.so`s **and** executables at `-O0` (CMake's default) and `-O2`. Every test dlopens both `.so`s and calls only exported symbols. `c_src/` is byte-for-byte untouched (md5s verified).\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n- **SYMBOLS.md** — 3 C symbols, **0 missing** from Rust (same kinds, `array` identical `0x100000` size). Machine-rechecked by `tests/symbols.rs`.\n- **ERRORS.md** — 40 rows from the C's only 2 rejection sites (the 3-term `||` split into its distinct glibc `strtoul` behaviours), each with a test.\n- **CONFIGS.md** — 39 rows; **no Cargo `[features]` exist**, so the cross-product verified is {no features} × {C -O0, -O2} × {Rust dev, release}.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n**SIGPIPE disposition.** With stdout/stderr on a pipe with no reader, the C dies from signal 13; Rust's runtime sets `SIG_IGN`, so it exited 1 instead. `src/main.rs` now restores `SIG_DFL`. Caught by `binary_cli.rs::cli_sigpipe_disposition`.\n\nTwo of my own documented expectations were also wrong (C and Rust agreed): `-18446744073709547521` wraps to 4095 not `UINT_MAX`, and `execve` with an empty argv is normalized by the kernel to `argc=1, argv[0]=\"\"` (true `argc==0`/NULL `argv[0]` is only reachable via FFI, where the C prints `(null)` and Rust matches).\n\n## Results\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| **Exhaustive** sweep of `perform_expensive_operations` | **all 4 294 967 296 `int` values** agree (16384 chunks, 16 shards) |\n| `.so` `main`, full 2000 iterations, seed 42 | rust `430392287` = c-O0 `430392287` = c-O2 `430392287` |\n| Real binaries, seeds 42/1/0 | identical stdout+stderr+status |\n| `rand`/`srand` port vs **real glibc** | 4096 random + all seeds 0..2047 + full 262144-draw fills |\n| `strtoul` validation vs **real glibc** | exhaustive all 1- and 2-byte args (65 280) + 100 000 random + boundary sweeps |\n| Whole suite (46 tests) | passes in `dev` (overflow-checks **on**) and `release` |\n\nAutomation: `scripts/check_features.sh`, `run_all.sh`, `exhaustive_sweep.sh`, `e2e_binaries.sh`. The only extra Rust exports are clearly-named `harness_*` hooks that call the same code the program uses — needed because the RNG and validation stages are otherwise only reachable behind a ~5-minute compute loop; nothing is stubbed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":253903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":965,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"994a44c2-98b6-4b9c-a7a9-508ed4953b92","uuid":"7011af71-da75-4566-b21d-a05e51e98725","timestamp":"2026-08-18T00:15:36.476Z"}
